e, the reason is applicable in principle, but the skewness is not clearly more extreme in one lottery over the other. The key is whether the individual considers the distribution of probability across outcomes to assess skewness. The reason is applicable because the structure of the lotteries allows for comparison of the probability weight on unfavorable outcomes.",
